## HUD (Tier 2 grammar)

Yes: tiny corner ticks, alignment markers, subtle crosshair intersections, understated grid/dot matrix, small section IDs, tiny telemetry labels, precision rulers/lines.

No: every card having `+` signs, every section looking like a SOC terminal, endless grids, neon outlines, sci-fi screen decoration.

HUD chrome is metadata and framing, not decoration. Use on evidence, diagrams, operational visualizations, coverage, security telemetry, Store technical product media. Not FAQ, forms, long prose, testimonials, editorial paper.

Maintenance Mode: **do not add HUD independently.** Vocabulary first (VIS-001 → VIS-002/003/004). See `design/HUD_CHROME.md`.

